GENESIS TODO
============

This document tracks features and improvements still needed for genesis.

Legend:
  [-] Partial / In Progress
  [ ] Not Started


================================================================================
PENDING FEATURES
================================================================================

Java 11:
  [ ] Annotations on lambda params with var: (@NonNull var x) -> x

Java 21:
  [ ] Record attribute parsing for positional component matching
      Currently pattern variable names must match record component names.
      Should read Record attribute from external class files for position-based matching.


================================================================================
DEFERRED / WILL NOT IMPLEMENT
================================================================================

  [ ] String templates (JEP 430, 459, 465)
      Withdrawn in Java 23 pending complete redesign.
      The template processor API was considered too complex and is being
      rethought. Wait for the redesigned feature in a future Java version.

  [ ] Primitive types in patterns (JEP 507)
      Still preview in Java 25. Revisit when finalized.

  [ ] Better error recovery in parser
      Basic recovery already exists (skip to ; or } on error).
      More sophisticated recovery (multiple errors, smarter sync points)
      would be useful for IDE integration but not critical for CLI use.


================================================================================
KNOWN BUGS
================================================================================

1. Ternary boxing in varargs (Conditional01-03):
   - Ternary expression results in varargs arrays get spurious Integer.valueOf()
   - Stack: [array, idx, String] but then calls Integer.valueOf expecting int
   - Issue in codegen_expr.c array element storage

2. Switch variable scoping (LambdaScope04 testSwitchLocal* tests):
   - Variables declared in case 0 used in default case
   - Genesis doesn't check for possibly-uninitialized variables

3. Varargs method reference with primitive array (MethodReference36):
   - Needs synthetic bridge method to wrap argument in Object[]
   - javac generates lambda$test$N methods that create Object[] wrapper

4. Type constraint violation detection (MethodReference68):
   - Compile-fail test - Genesis doesn't detect the error
   - Generates invalid bytecode instead of compile error

5. Lambda cast to primitive type (TargetType17):
   - Compile-fail test - should error but doesn't

6. Generic constructor Signature attribute:
   - Uses return type instead of V

7. Arrays of type variables from class files (N[] fields):
   - A field or parameter typed N[] where N extends Number, loaded from a
     class file rather than source, is referenced as Object[] instead of
     Number[]. Bare type variables are handled.

8. Nested interface methods are registered twice in semantic analysis
   (once without and once with the implicit public abstract modifiers).
   Consumers such as the functional interface lookup deduplicate by name;
   the double registration itself should be removed.

9. A boxed-LHS compound assignment (Integer i; i += 1;) unboxes, promotes
    and reboxes correctly for a local variable, field or array element, but
    only because codegen_compound_rhs handles it generically; it has not
    been separately tested with a wrapper of every primitive type.

10. -sourcepath compiles more files than javac would, for a real (not
    cosmetic) reason: scan_package_for_type() (semantic.c) - the fallback
    used to find a same-package type referenced by simple name with no
    import - scans and loads every .java file in the matching package
    directory before it reaches the one that declares the type actually
    being looked up (or gives up having found nothing), and
    load_class_from_source_impl()'s "track this file as a dependency"
    step fires unconditionally for every file it parses, including ones
    loaded only to rule them out - even when resolving a completely
    unrelated bare identifier (e.g. "System"). A fix was attempted
    (suppress the generic per-file tracking during a scan, explicitly
    queue only the file a lookup actually confirms it needs) but
    reverted: same-package type resolution turns out to be reimplemented
    independently in at least 4 separate places in semantic.c (in
    lookup_same_package_type()'s own cache-hit path, a duplicate direct
    hashtable_lookup(sem->types, ...) check in method-call target-class
    resolution, and at least one more for parameter/field type resolution
    via resolve_unresolved_type()/the shared type registry, never fully
    traced to its exact call site), each bypassing a single-choke-point
    fix differently. Fixing 3 of the 4 got a simple repro working but
    broke SamePackageSourcepathTest (NoClassDefFoundError on types used
    only as parameter types, resolved through the 4th, untraced path).
    Needs either auditing all the duplicate resolution paths individually,
    or consolidating them to all go through lookup_same_package_type().

11. A JDK with no jmods directory (JDK 24+ builds such as Eclipse Temurin 25,
    JEP 493) cannot be used: jdk_detect_from_path() in classpath.c accepts
    lib/modules as the module source, but nothing reads it (it is a jimage
    file, not a directory of .jmod archives), so every java.* type is
    unresolved. Needs a jimage reader (header, redirect/offset tables,
    location attributes, and /packages and /modules entries to map a
    package to its module), or a fallback to jrt-fs.jar / the java launcher.
    Until then the README states the requirement, and CI uses a JDK that
    ships jmods.

12. -parameters is accepted but no MethodParameters attribute is written, so
    reflection reports arg0, arg1... for genesis-compiled classes. Spring
    (6.1 and later) finds parameter names only that way; code compiled with
    genesis loses @RequestParam-style name inference.

13. make smoke-spring-boot (bench/spring-boot/): with javac, all of core/,
    module/ and test-support/ of Spring Boot v4.1.1 compiles except
    spring-boot-gradle-test-support (it needs Gradle TestKit) and 15,055 of
    15,700 tests pass (the rest need annotation processing, a container or a
    port). Genesis compiles every source set, but only 12,205 of those
    15,055 tests pass. Left: Spring application contexts that fail to start
    (the largest group, each from some underlying codegen or annotation bug),
    ClassCastException Long -> Integer in PropertyMapper users, missing
    parameter names (item 12), type-use annotations written in modifier
    position ("@Nullable String") not emitted as type annotations, and
    NoSuchMethodError on constructors of nested classes. Iterate with
    SB_COMPILERS=genesis SB_KEEP=1 and compare against the javac reports.

================================================================================
OPTIONAL IMPROVEMENTS
================================================================================

Refactoring:
  - Split codegen_expr.c (7600+ lines) into smaller modules
  - Replace remaining slist_new/slist_append patterns with slist_push
  - Consider moving resolve_java_lang_class to a utility module

Inner class synthetic accessors:
  - Nested classes reach each other's private members through nestmates
    (class file version 55, Java 11+). With an explicit -target below 11 the
    NestHost/NestMembers attributes are omitted, so private access between
    nested classes fails at run time. Full support for older targets would
    generate synthetic access$N methods, as javac does for -target 8.
